{
    "background_story": "Isaias was a brilliant linguist known for his groundbreaking research on the intricacies of language. His obsession with the concept of anacoluthia, a rhetorical device in which a sentence or phrase is begun in one way and finished in another, led him to spend years studying the works of ancient Greek and Roman orators. As he delved deeper into his research, Isaias became fascinated by the ways in which anacoluthia could be used to convey complex emotions and ideas. He began to experiment with the device in his own writing, crafting sentences that twisted and turned in unexpected ways. His unique style earned him both acclaim and criticism, but Isaias remained undeterred, convinced that the art of anacoluthia held the key to unlocking new forms of literary expression.",
